    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d833">

                <pb facs="0899" n="887" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg887"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">661.6431/10–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Representative in Hungary</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schoenfeld</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-13T14:00:00-05:00">October 13, 1945—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>535. Your 746 and 747 Oct. 11. Dept considers that Soviet-Hungarian economic
                    collaboration agreement is not properly matter for ACC decision but rather for
                    consideration at governmental level among three principal Allied powers. It does
                    not believe therefore that Key should request inclusion of this matter on ACC
                    agenda. However, if question of agreement is discussed in ACC meeting, substance
                        <pb facs="0900" n="888" xml:id="pg888"/> of Dept’s tel of Oct 13 to Moscow
                    rpted to you as 536<anchor n="14" xml:id="d833-f1"/> may be used by Key to
                    indicate US position. This Govt could not of course agree to Voroshilov’s taking
                    any positive action on this question in name of ACC without consent of US and
                    Brit reps on that body. Sent Budapest rptd Moscow and London.<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d833-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d833-f1" n="14" xml:id="d833-f1-content">
                <p>Same as telegram 2159 to Moscow, <hi rendition="#italic">infra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d833-f2" n="15" xml:id="d833-f2-content">
                <p>Repeated to Moscow as No. 2158 and to London as No. 9104.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
